WEBVTT

00:02.437 --> 00:05.669
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.774 --> 00:09.041
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.146 --> 00:12.446
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.551 --> 00:15.317
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.856 --> 00:19.088
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.194 --> 00:22.427
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.532 --> 00:23.864
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.968 --> 00:25.731
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.837 --> 00:31.745
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:35.251 --> 00:37.880
Hey, Quagmire,
how was your date last night?

00:38.021 --> 00:40.889
Cleveland, it was amazing.
You know what I discovered last night?

00:40.992 --> 00:42.961
- Women have a fourth hole.
- What?

00:43.062 --> 00:46.260
Yeah. I mean, it's only visible if you're
looking from exactly the right angle,

00:46.367 --> 00:50.498
like the entrance to Hogwarts.
But you got to believe that it's there.

00:50.606 --> 00:54.544
Man, I envy you single guys.
No families, partying whenever you want.

00:54.645 --> 00:57.615
These are the only people
I get to party with.

00:57.784 --> 00:59.445
That's where the fourth hole
is, right there.

00:59.552 --> 01:01.077
Right there in the back of the knee.

01:01.188 --> 01:05.889
I like having a family. I got all the crazy
out of my system when I was 18.

01:05.995 --> 01:10.161
Not me. I was dating Lois the whole time.
I never got to be wild.

01:10.268 --> 01:12.965
Except for that time I rode
the mechanical bull at that bar.

01:14.841 --> 01:19.439
Oh, my God, how embarrassing!
Look how much fun I am!

01:20.349 --> 01:22.841
It's like I missed out on half my life.

01:22.953 --> 01:26.856
What I wouldn't give to be 18 again,
like those kids on spring break.

01:26.959 --> 01:28.756
<i>Grim news from Daytona, Florida,</i>

01:28.861 --> 01:30.955
<i>where the remains of
three female college students</i>

01:31.064 --> 01:33.124
<i>were found near a local nightclub.</i>

01:33.234 --> 01:35.829
<i>Reports suggest that
all three were violated sexually</i>

01:35.939 --> 01:37.566
<i>before being brutally murdered.</i>

01:37.674 --> 01:40.736
Oh, man, see that?
Everybody's getting laid but me.

01:42.147 --> 01:43.615
Oh, come on!

01:44.650 --> 01:46.585
Hang on, I'll fix it.

01:48.056 --> 01:51.117
Oh, my God, is he dead?
I think he might be dead!

01:51.227 --> 01:55.131
Oh, did you hear that?
Noah Wyle here thinks he might be dead.

01:55.233 --> 01:58.864
Step aside, junior.
Nope, he's just knocked out.

01:58.972 --> 02:03.001
Damn, I drove all the way out here.
I had to cancel another appointment.

02:03.111 --> 02:05.342
I never like to be too far away
from Mike Wallace.

02:13.492 --> 02:16.360
Hey, Death, I got a favor to ask you.

02:16.464 --> 02:19.628
Could you let me go back in time
and be 18 again?

02:19.735 --> 02:21.465
What, are you high? No.

02:21.571 --> 02:23.597
<i>Coming up next on ESPN,</i>

02:23.707 --> 02:25.801
<i>- Women's Professional...
- All right, you win.</i>

02:25.911 --> 02:28.779
Let's go. But just for one night.

02:39.463 --> 02:42.456
- What the hell? Where are we?
- Oh, my God, this is...

02:42.567 --> 02:45.868
This is Newport Country Club.
I used to be a towel boy here.

02:45.973 --> 02:48.408
That's right, Peter.
You're 18 years old again.

02:48.510 --> 02:50.536
At least, that's how everyone will see you.

02:52.549 --> 02:55.314
Hey, Peter, slap me five.

02:55.420 --> 02:56.978
Slap me ten.

02:57.089 --> 02:58.488
Around the side.

02:58.590 --> 03:00.115
And back again.

03:00.226 --> 03:01.454
Up high.

03:01.562 --> 03:02.859
Down low.

03:02.964 --> 03:06.231
Now, over by the diving board.

03:06.936 --> 03:09.098
Now, on the other side of the pool.

03:12.043 --> 03:15.173
All right, now, I want you to meet me
at this address in an hour,

03:15.282 --> 03:16.874
and we'll slap five there.

03:16.984 --> 03:20.183
- Then afterwards, we'll hit the bars.
- That sounds good to me.

03:20.289 --> 03:22.485
I'm 18, and I'm ready to do some living.

03:22.592 --> 03:24.891
<i>We are gonna raise more hell
than Hellraiser.</i>

03:27.532 --> 03:30.229
Hey, honey, you want
some salt for your steak?

03:30.336 --> 03:31.998
Yeah, sure.

03:33.208 --> 03:35.837
Gotcha! That's more salt than you wanted.

03:36.479 --> 03:38.209
Hello, boys.

03:44.524 --> 03:47.517
Wow, 18-year-old Lois.

03:48.162 --> 03:49.824
Son of a bitch.

03:59.712 --> 04:04.778
<i>I see those ivory lies
in sweet Rosita's eyes</i>

04:04.887 --> 04:11.067
<i>Gonna leave them both behind
when we Tomaso all night</i>

04:14.076 --> 04:15.338
Hi, Peter.

04:15.444 --> 04:17.811
I'm really looking forward to
the movie tonight.

04:17.914 --> 04:19.815
<i>Peter and I are going to see Zapped.</i>

04:19.917 --> 04:22.011
I figured Scott Baio was
androgynous enough

04:22.120 --> 04:24.955
that we could both fantasize about him,
and no one would be gay.

04:25.059 --> 04:28.393
Lois, we got the rest of our lives
for me to not hear a word you just said,

04:28.496 --> 04:29.623
but tonight, I got plans with Cleveland.

04:31.300 --> 04:33.292
But we had a date.

04:33.938 --> 04:34.927
I would eat your poo.

04:39.389 --> 04:41.381
<i>Stay tuned for President Ronald Reagan's</i>

04:41.492 --> 04:42.754
<i>weekly radio address.</i>

04:42.928 --> 04:46.729
Ronald Reagan? The actor?
He's President?

04:46.833 --> 04:49.530
Peter, you're the one from the future.
You should know... Ah, forget it.

04:49.638 --> 04:53.268
Oh, you've got to hear
this new Eddie Murphy cassette I bought.

04:53.376 --> 04:55.470
<i>Hey, did you ever
have a barbecue?</i>

04:56.581 --> 04:57.843
I have!

05:02.889 --> 05:04.858
Wow, you're really good at this game.

05:04.959 --> 05:08.226
Yeah, I've logged a lot of game hours
on Menstrual Miss Pacman.

05:10.401 --> 05:11.493
- What? What?
- Jeez.

05:11.602 --> 05:12.592
- Nothing.
- Bitch.

05:14.458 --> 05:16.984
<i>So, have you seen Ghostbusters?</i>

05:17.095 --> 05:19.826
Save your breath, geekwad.
I'm here with my boyfriend.

05:19.932 --> 05:23.369
You mean that quintessentially '80s guy
with his collar turned up all the way?

05:23.471 --> 05:27.101
- Are you hitting on my girlfriend?
- No, no, I was just being friendly.

05:27.209 --> 05:30.203
I will kick your ass anytime, anywhere.

05:31.081 --> 05:33.414
Okay, how about
top of the World Trade Center,

05:33.518 --> 05:36.215
the morning of September 11th, 2001,
8:00 a. M?

05:36.322 --> 05:38.587
I'll be there.
You think I'll forget, but I won't.

05:41.841 --> 05:43.901
- That was nice.
- I'll say.

05:44.011 --> 05:46.003
Peter, is that... Are you...

05:46.114 --> 05:48.242
- Molly Ringwald?
- Yeah. How's it going?

05:48.351 --> 05:51.344
Wow, you're the biggest star in the
world right now. What are you doing here?

05:51.455 --> 05:53.390
Oh, I like to hook up
with random bar guys.

05:53.758 --> 05:55.590
Lucky for me, huh?

05:55.995 --> 05:57.623
No, a hobby's good.

05:57.731 --> 05:59.461
All right, Peter, your time's up.

05:59.567 --> 06:02.036
- Oh, man, already?
- Yup, come on.

06:03.872 --> 06:06.843
Good to meet you, Molly.
I'll be back later for your career.

06:11.484 --> 06:15.388
- Well, I hope you got your fill, Peter.
- Death, that was totally worth it.

06:15.490 --> 06:16.616
It was even better than the time

06:16.724 --> 06:19.091
I stumbled into
that fat, lonely women's club.

06:20.864 --> 06:23.891
Excuse me, could I get directions
to the Providence Civic Center?

06:27.140 --> 06:29.200
- Do you like cake?
- Yes.

06:29.310 --> 06:31.802
- Do you like my ass?
- Yes.

06:31.913 --> 06:34.212
Do you want to eat cake off my ass?

06:34.317 --> 06:37.685
- What kind of cake?
- Angel food cake.

06:38.323 --> 06:42.261
Well, Rusty, looks like we're gonna
eat our way out of another jam.

07:00.120 --> 07:02.089
- Honey, you awake?
- Morning, sweetie.

07:03.292 --> 07:05.386
Who the hell are you?
What are you doing in my bed?

07:05.495 --> 07:08.294
Peter, it's me, Molly. Your wife?

07:08.399 --> 07:10.960
Molly Ringwald? You're my wife?

07:11.069 --> 07:13.869
We've been married for 20 years.
What's wrong with you?

07:13.974 --> 07:17.706
Hi. I'm Judd Nelson.
I crash here once or twice a week.

07:24.822 --> 07:28.351
Brian, Molly Ringwald is in my bed,
and she says she's my wife!

07:28.461 --> 07:31.727
That's not all.
Look at this place. Everything's different.

07:31.833 --> 07:33.198
This is crazy.

07:33.301 --> 07:35.793
<i>Brian, did you ever see
that Twilight Zone episode?</i>

07:35.905 --> 07:37.464
You know, where the woman wakes up
in the hospital,

07:37.574 --> 07:38.803
and all the doctors are pigs?

07:38.910 --> 07:40.707
- Yeah.
- I like that one.

07:40.812 --> 07:44.250
- But what the hell is going on here?
- You know, I think I have a theory.

07:44.351 --> 07:46.718
It's possible that
when we went back in time,

07:46.821 --> 07:48.881
we somehow altered the past.

07:48.991 --> 07:50.550
Jeez, Brian, that's more ridiculous

07:50.660 --> 07:53.596
than the theory of
why Tom Cruise runs in all his movies.

07:55.867 --> 07:58.428
Wow, that cameraman
has nice, strong arms.

07:59.740 --> 08:02.539
You can't catch me, gay thoughts.

08:04.146 --> 08:05.910
- Hey, where the hell is Lois?
- That's weird.

08:06.016 --> 08:07.005
Looks like she's coming out
of Quagmire's house.

08:10.173 --> 08:11.299
Lois, what the hell?

08:11.407 --> 08:13.933
I'm gone for one night,
and you sleep with Quagmire?

08:14.044 --> 08:18.142
Mr. Griffin, what I do with my husband
is none of your business.

08:18.250 --> 08:19.809
- Husband?
- Morning, Pete.

08:19.920 --> 08:22.185
Hope you and Molly can still join us
for dinner tonight.

08:22.290 --> 08:24.088
Come here, baby. Let's head upstairs
and play hide-and-go-anal.

08:27.215 --> 08:28.513
Brian, what the hell is going on?

08:28.617 --> 08:32.885
We were only in 1984 one night,
and now everything's all messed up.

08:32.990 --> 08:35.323
I think I can explain it to you, Peter.

08:35.794 --> 08:38.320
This line represents
the normal flow of events.

08:38.431 --> 08:40.525
Here's where you met Lois,
here's where you got married,

08:40.634 --> 08:43.763
and here's the present.
And here's the night at the bar.

08:44.006 --> 08:45.667
Now, at some point during that evening,

08:45.775 --> 08:48.405
you did something
that changed the course of your history,

08:48.513 --> 08:51.972
causing the time line to skew off
into an alternate tangent,

08:52.084 --> 08:55.544
where you're married to Molly Ringwald,
Quagmire's married to Lois,

08:55.690 --> 08:57.921
and for some reason,
we have a chalkboard in the living room.

08:58.026 --> 08:59.459
Well, what are we gonna do?

08:59.561 --> 09:02.691
We got to figure out what happened
at this point in time.

09:02.800 --> 09:04.792
And I'll tell you another thing
that worries me.

09:04.903 --> 09:07.702
You ever hear the theory that
if you kill a butterfly in the past,

09:07.807 --> 09:11.677
it can drastically alter the present?
Well, who knows what else we changed.

09:12.380 --> 09:13.973
<i>Tonight,
on The Tonight Show,</i>

09:14.083 --> 09:15.984
<i>movie star, George Clooney.</i>

09:16.086 --> 09:18.954
<i>- Oh, he's good.
Comedian, Dave Chappelle.</i>

09:19.056 --> 09:20.115
He's funny. Like him.

09:20.225 --> 09:22.660
<i>And musician,
Harry Connick Jr.</i>

09:22.762 --> 09:24.093
Wow, what a show.

09:24.197 --> 09:28.135
<i>And now,
ladies and gentlemen, here's...</i>

09:28.236 --> 09:29.226
<i>Chevy!</i>

09:29.338 --> 09:32.502
Oh, God, Brian, we messed up bad.
We messed up real bad.

09:37.116 --> 09:40.713
Howdy, neighbors. Come on in.
Hey, Lois, Peter and Molly are here!

09:40.821 --> 09:42.756
Chris, say hi to Mr. And Mrs. Griffin.

09:42.858 --> 09:45.225
- Hi, Mr. Griffin.
- How's it going, man?

09:45.328 --> 09:46.990
Chris, Stewie!

09:47.097 --> 09:49.088
Oh, my God!
All right, don't freak out, Peter.

09:49.199 --> 09:51.726
Don't freak out like you did
when your goldfish died.

09:52.004 --> 09:54.872
Here you go, Lieutenant Shiny-Sides.

09:54.975 --> 09:57.774
It's okay. You don't have to eat it now.

09:57.879 --> 10:01.282
You're just sleeping. You'll eat it later.

10:01.384 --> 10:04.752
You'll eat it later, Lieutenant Shiny-Sides!

10:10.531 --> 10:13.194
Meg, stop staring at Mr. Griffin.

10:13.301 --> 10:16.795
I'm sorry, Peter.
I'm afraid she's got her father's libido.

10:16.907 --> 10:19.035
What can I say? I'm a Vagitarius. Oh!

10:20.779 --> 10:23.271
- Giggity Giggity Giggity.
- Giggity Giggity Giggity.

10:23.383 --> 10:25.750
Hey, did you guys hear on the news
about President Gore

10:25.853 --> 10:28.846
hunting down and killing
Osama bin Laden with his bare hands?

10:28.957 --> 10:33.658
<i>I know. Who would've thought bin Laden
was hiding out in the cast of Mad TV?</i>

10:33.764 --> 10:36.393
Man, the perfect hiding spot.
The one place no one would look.

10:37.603 --> 10:39.435
Oh, there's the pie.

10:42.743 --> 10:46.579
- Lois, this is a huge mistake.
- What are you talking about, Peter?

10:46.683 --> 10:48.447
You're supposed to be married to me.

10:48.552 --> 10:51.044
We're the ones who were meant to
be together, not you and Quagmire.

10:52.257 --> 10:54.727
It's a little late for that,
don't you think, Peter?

10:54.828 --> 10:56.820
I mean, there was a time
back when we dated

10:56.931 --> 10:59.492
that I thought you might be the one,

10:59.602 --> 11:03.665
but as I recall, you were more
interested in partying with your friends.

11:03.774 --> 11:07.370
Then Glenn came along
and stole my heart.

11:07.479 --> 11:10.507
When he kissed me that night
at the Country Club Dance,

11:10.618 --> 11:12.883
I knew we'd be together forever.

11:12.988 --> 11:16.516
Hey, Lois, I'm ready for your pie.
And you made dessert, too! Oh!

11:16.626 --> 11:21.224
Oh, Glenn, I love all your sex jokes
and your dirty puns.

11:21.332 --> 11:23.392
That's why I married you.

11:23.870 --> 11:26.863
- Let's go upstairs and do it.
- Okay!

11:31.781 --> 11:34.512
Brian, going back in time ruined my life.

11:34.618 --> 11:38.852
We've got to get Death to send us back
to 1984 again, so I can undo what I did.

11:38.958 --> 11:42.691
Or we could just make the best of this.
Al Gore is President.

11:42.797 --> 11:45.358
We could kind of just take that one
and call it a win.

11:45.467 --> 11:48.996
I mean, with Bush, we didn't have
flying cars that run on vegetable oil.

11:51.143 --> 11:53.635
<i>Meet George Jetson</i>

11:56.951 --> 11:58.442
<i>His boy Elroy</i>

12:03.060 --> 12:04.551
<i>Daughter Judy</i>

12:09.035 --> 12:11.163
<i>Jane his wife</i>

12:12.840 --> 12:14.035
Hey, hey, hey! No, no, no, no, no.

12:16.859 --> 12:21.093
I took this one out for you.
You take this one, I keep this!

12:21.199 --> 12:23.862
You are not taking my whole wallet
so you can go shopping.

12:23.969 --> 12:25.301
I was just going to buy some groceries.

12:25.405 --> 12:26.394
Bullshit.

12:29.720 --> 12:32.986
I don't care what it takes, Brian,
I've got to get Lois back somehow.

12:33.091 --> 12:34.957
Well, the only one
who can help us is Death,

12:35.061 --> 12:37.030
and he only shows up
when somebody dies.

12:37.130 --> 12:38.291
That's gonna be tough.

12:38.399 --> 12:40.060
With President Gore's
universal health care,

12:40.168 --> 12:41.761
people are living much longer these days.

12:41.870 --> 12:43.532
And with zero-tolerance gun control

12:43.640 --> 12:46.940
and a strong, well-funded educational
system, there's no street crime.

12:47.179 --> 12:48.840
Face it, Peter, you not marrying Lois

12:48.947 --> 12:50.779
was the best thing
that ever happened to the world.

12:50.883 --> 12:54.218
I don't care. We've got to find a way
to summon Death and quick.

12:56.759 --> 12:58.728
Well, that might do it.

12:59.162 --> 13:00.858
Death! Oh, thank God, you're here!

13:00.965 --> 13:04.402
Listen, you've got to send me
back in time again, so I can marry Lois.

13:04.503 --> 13:06.028
Man, it's been a busy day.

13:06.139 --> 13:07.903
Dick Cheney, the chairman of Halliburton,

13:08.009 --> 13:11.138
shot Supreme Court Justice Scalia
in a hunting accident,

13:11.246 --> 13:15.207
and the bullet went right through him
and killed Karl Rove and Tucker Carlson.

13:15.319 --> 13:19.417
- Oh, my God, Peter, you can't marry Lois.
- I don't know who any of those people are.

13:23.798 --> 13:26.290
All right, hang on. Here we go.

13:31.976 --> 13:36.108
This is the exact moment in 1984
that I sent you to the first time.

13:36.215 --> 13:38.275
You've just got to manage
not to screw it up again.

13:40.522 --> 13:43.014
Lois! Oh, my God, it's so good to see you!

13:43.125 --> 13:45.823
<i>Hey, Peter, you all set
to go see Zapped tonight?</i>

13:45.930 --> 13:48.058
I figured Scott Baio was
androgynous enough that we...

13:48.167 --> 13:49.657
That we could both fantasize about him

13:49.768 --> 13:51.361
and no one would be gay,
yeah, I know the joke.

13:51.471 --> 13:52.905
<i>Hey, you know what?
Listen, Zapped sucks.</i>

13:53.007 --> 13:54.338
<i>Why don't we go see Krull?</i>

13:54.442 --> 13:58.471
<i>- Peter, you know I'm dying to see Zapped.
- I would much prefer Krull.</i>

13:58.581 --> 14:00.709
Well, maybe you should
just go by yourself.

14:00.818 --> 14:02.946
- Well, maybe I will.
- Fine.

14:03.188 --> 14:04.850
Crap. Death!

14:04.957 --> 14:06.653
- What?
- One more time.

14:07.327 --> 14:10.126
<i>Hey, Peter, you all set
to go see Zapped tonight?</i>

14:10.231 --> 14:12.827
I figured Scott Baio was
androgynous enough that we...

14:13.536 --> 14:18.134
<i>That's hilarious! You are a delight.
And Zapped is one of my favorite movies.</i>

14:18.243 --> 14:20.439
I look forward to watching it
with you, sweetheart.

14:20.546 --> 14:21.878
Oh, wonderful.

14:23.450 --> 14:24.713
Death!

14:24.819 --> 14:27.653
<i>Hey, Peter, you all set
to go see Zapped tonight?</i>

14:27.756 --> 14:28.951
- I figured Scott Baio...
- Yes.

14:29.059 --> 14:31.221
Scott Baio, gay, blah, blah, blah, blah.

14:31.462 --> 14:35.491
- I can't wait to see the movie.
- Well, terrific. I'll see you tonight.

14:35.602 --> 14:36.762
Oh, hey, Peter.

14:36.870 --> 14:40.330
Say, I was just getting ready to
hit the town. You want to join me?

14:40.442 --> 14:42.570
I can't, Cleveland, I got a date with Lois.

14:42.678 --> 14:45.705
- It's gonna to be fun.
- It is?

15:00.137 --> 15:02.504
Peter, what the hell are you doing?
You're supposed to be with Lois.

15:02.607 --> 15:04.404
Aw, crap! Death!

15:04.911 --> 15:07.312
No! You know what?
I'm not doing it again.

15:07.414 --> 15:10.316
Screw this. No more mulligans.
You're on your own.

15:10.752 --> 15:13.449
Oh, damn it, Brian,
what the hell am I gonna do now?

15:13.556 --> 15:17.221
I haven't screwed up this bad since
I bought Joe Piscopo that barbell set.

15:17.628 --> 15:20.565
All right, Joe,
now don't get carried away with this.

15:20.667 --> 15:24.160
Don't worry, Peter.
I'll only work out during my downtime.

15:29.078 --> 15:32.208
Oh, look who it is. Only 14 hours late.

15:32.317 --> 15:34.684
If you don't want to spend time
with me, Peter, that's fine.

15:34.787 --> 15:37.018
But at least don't make me
wait up all night for you.

15:37.123 --> 15:39.991
Lois, I'm so sorry.
I promise, I'll make it up to you tonight.

15:40.094 --> 15:41.960
We can watch any stupid movie you want.

15:42.064 --> 15:46.435
- Sorry, I've already got plans.
- What do you mean, "plans"?

15:46.537 --> 15:49.132
I'm going to the Country Club Dance
with Glenn.

15:49.241 --> 15:51.506
I wanted to surprise you
with the invitation last night,

15:51.611 --> 15:53.079
but you never showed up.

15:53.180 --> 15:55.706
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I have to get ready.

15:56.452 --> 16:00.219
Peter, the Country Club Dance is where
Lois said she fell in love with Quagmire.

16:00.323 --> 16:02.224
If they kiss at that dance, you're finished.

16:02.326 --> 16:04.022
You're right, Brian.
We've got to stop them.

16:04.129 --> 16:07.031
And I think I know how.

16:15.045 --> 16:16.637
- Peter!
- Oh, God, sorry! Sorry!

16:16.748 --> 16:18.443
Sorry. You're right, let's go to the dance.

16:24.206 --> 16:26.266
Peter used to be so passionate.

16:26.376 --> 16:29.346
Suddenly, he just doesn't seem
very interested in me anymore.

16:29.447 --> 16:33.385
Lois, if I may speak freely, as a friend,
you deserve better than Peter.

16:33.486 --> 16:37.447
- You deserve a gentleman.
- Oh, Glenn, you're so sweet.

16:37.559 --> 16:39.755
- Oh! Something poked me.
- It's okay, it's okay.

16:39.862 --> 16:40.851
It's just my penis.

16:49.763 --> 16:52.130
Now I know what a TV dinner feels like.

16:52.233 --> 16:54.429
<i>What?
- It's a line from Die Hard.</i>

16:54.536 --> 16:56.937
Hasn't been made yet.
We could write it, Brian.

16:57.040 --> 16:59.009
After we're done with this,
we could write it.

17:01.146 --> 17:03.411
Oh, my God! You just crushed Andy!

17:03.516 --> 17:06.487
- Oh, yeah, sorry about that.
- Oh, oh, you're sorry?

17:06.588 --> 17:08.351
Who's gonna play guitar?

17:14.065 --> 17:17.867
<i>Earth angel, earth angel</i>

17:18.338 --> 17:20.330
Oh, I love this song.

17:22.177 --> 17:24.578
<i>My darling dear</i>

17:24.680 --> 17:29.176
- Lois, may I have this dance?
- Peter, what are you doing here?

17:29.287 --> 17:31.017
I love you, Lois Pewterschmidt.

17:31.123 --> 17:32.954
And not Quagmire, or any man,

17:33.058 --> 17:36.587
she-male, robot or sentient robot
curious about its own existence,

17:36.697 --> 17:39.826
- is gonna keep you from me!
- Peter, I am here with Glenn.

17:39.935 --> 17:41.995
You had your chance with me
and you blew it.

17:42.105 --> 17:43.937
Now, leave us alone.

17:44.041 --> 17:47.911
- Is that what you really want, Lois?
- Yes, it is.

17:48.481 --> 17:50.643
Well, I guess that's it.

17:50.751 --> 17:54.314
Who the hell am I kidding?
I don't deserve her.

17:59.263 --> 18:02.894
Come on, Peter.
Prove to Lois that you love her.

18:03.002 --> 18:04.903
It's your last chance.

18:08.844 --> 18:10.779
Hey, Quagmire.
- Huh?

18:15.753 --> 18:18.519
Sorry, Lois, but I have to do this.

18:22.597 --> 18:26.433
Oh, Peter, that was so passionate.

18:26.536 --> 18:28.835
Why, I didn't know
I meant that much to you.

18:28.939 --> 18:32.536
Are you kidding?
Lois, I couldn't bear to live without you.

18:32.645 --> 18:35.809
I came back thinking
I was missing something in my life,

18:35.916 --> 18:39.786
but what I almost missed was
the best thing that's ever happened to me.

18:39.889 --> 18:43.418
Lois Pewterschmidt, will you be my wife?

18:44.362 --> 18:47.161
Yes. Yes, I will.

18:48.067 --> 18:51.037
<i>Earth angel, earth angel</i>

18:51.672 --> 18:54.802
<i>Please be mine</i>

18:55.278 --> 18:57.372
<i>My darling dear</i>

18:57.481 --> 19:01.544
<i>I'll love you for all time</i>

19:01.654 --> 19:04.624
<i>I'm just a fool</i>

19:04.724 --> 19:09.288
<i>A fool in love with you</i>

19:19.045 --> 19:21.037
I think they want another one.

19:23.484 --> 19:25.977
Uh, okay.

19:28.626 --> 19:30.355
<i>Here's a song by a gay guy.</i>

19:39.174 --> 19:42.236
<i>We're no strangers to love</i>

19:43.113 --> 19:46.607
<i>You know the rules and so do I</i>

19:47.353 --> 19:51.291
<i>A full commitment's what I'm thinking of</i>

19:51.392 --> 19:55.194
<i>You wouldn't get this from any other guy</i>

19:55.298 --> 19:59.703
<i>I just want to tell you how I'm feeling</i>

20:00.472 --> 20:02.873
<i>Got to make you understand</i>

20:02.975 --> 20:07.038
<i>Never gonna give you up
Never gonna let you down</i>

20:07.148 --> 20:08.810
<i>Never gonna run around...</i>

20:08.917 --> 20:10.612
Whoa, whoa, big guy.

20:10.719 --> 20:12.654
You're probably never even
gonna see him again.

20:13.290 --> 20:15.349
<i>Never gonna say good-bye</i>

20:15.460 --> 20:19.727
<i>Never gonna tell a lie and hurt you</i>

20:19.832 --> 20:22.860
Hey, Rick, it's your cousin, Marvin.

20:22.971 --> 20:24.940
Marvin Astley.

20:25.041 --> 20:28.910
You know that mediocre,
generic sound you've been looking for?

20:29.013 --> 20:30.640
Well, listen to this!

20:30.748 --> 20:32.239
<i>Never gonna give
Never gonna give</i>

20:32.351 --> 20:34.650
<i>Give you up</i>

20:34.754 --> 20:36.552
<i>Never gonna give
Never gonna give</i>

20:36.657 --> 20:38.455
<i>Give you up</i>

20:39.127 --> 20:42.120
<i>Never gonna give</i>

20:54.383 --> 20:56.318
I didn't like any of that.

21:00.124 --> 21:03.425
Wow, Peter, that's an amazing story.

21:03.529 --> 21:07.865
And I'm touched that you went through
so much trouble just to be with me.

21:07.969 --> 21:10.962
Obviously, I made the right choice
when I married you.

21:11.107 --> 21:12.507
Me, too, Lois.

21:12.609 --> 21:14.407
And, hey, let's just all be grateful

21:14.512 --> 21:17.243
that things are completely
back to normal again.

21:17.349 --> 21:19.784
Who ate all the pecan sandies?

21:19.785 --> 22:20.785
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru